msgid ""
"Replace 6E2F4E7AF50A5827 with your key ID, preferably the **long keyID** "
"which is the last 16 hex digits of the long number in the second line of the "
"output above:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:85 f38a293f46d54b45be5aa8f2013bab07
msgid "Using PGP with Git"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:88 190c711f03844b5aafcb41b2cde462e8
msgid ""
"If you’re submitting a patch via GitHub (or a similar Git server), please "
"sign your Git commits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:90 bbd3e58a4aaf4d3596a2331b9d610ca6
msgid "Set up Git to use your key:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:98 71d4eccc81394a3594fc9c883684c6f2
msgid "Set up Git to sign your commits with your key:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:105
#: 4bc8f7e9ad164fbfa62cc31cd8eb63a2
msgid "Alternatively, manually specify when a commit is to be signed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:113
#: 6535b599c8284c20885ff1ef0fabb9fb
msgid ""
"(Optional) Create signed tags. Signed commits are totally sufficient to "
"contribute to Qubes OS. However, if you have commits which are not signed "
"and you do not want to change them, you can create a signed tag for the "
"commit and push it before the check."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:115
#: 30bb8301856a454ba63f7060948d0a6b
msgid ""
"This is useful for example, if you have a commit back in the git history "
"which you like to sign now without rewriting the history."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:122
#: 6b01a7720fe74a168e172e40f8177569
msgid ""
"You can also create an alias to make this easier. Edit your ``~/.gitconfig`` "
"file. In the ``[alias]`` section, add ``stag`` to create signed tags and "
"``spush`` to create signed tags and push them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:131
#: 487a7a8fea7447b589343d7b893e2199
msgid ""
"You may also find it convenient to have an alias for verifying the tag on "
"the latest commit:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:142
#: 8698511da1cf475ab882eb58a9cf22aa
msgid "GitHub Signature Verification (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:145
#: 29dc1a72853a4d00b7b0fb95edbe00bc
msgid ""
"GitHub shows a green ``Verified`` label indicating that the GPG signature "
"could be verified using any of the contributor’s GPG keys uploaded to "
"GitHub. You can upload your public key on GitHub by adding your public GPG "
"key on the `New GPG key <https://github.com/settings/gpg/new>`__ under the "
"`SSH GPG keys page <https://github.com/settings/keys>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:148
#: a0bf58fc5949452b883d7cda7662db88
msgid "Code Signature Checks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:151
#: 3bb50848472a475abc4e5036b006e2d4
msgid ""
"The `signature-checker <https://github.com/marmarek/signature-checker>`__ "
"checks if code contributions are signed. Although GitHub adds a little green "
"``Verified`` button next to the commit, the `signature-checker <https://"
"github.com/marmarek/signature-checker>`__ uses this algorithm to check if a "
"commit is correctly signed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:153
#: 6147b82366dc48459ee480e91082f644
msgid ""
"Is the commit signed? If the commit is not signed, you can see the message"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:155
#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:167
#: 77b71f6dbca246318fa84e2b15fa343f 77decf3d4c1944a59dd0f581d1c6e2d0
msgid "``policy/qubesos/code-signing — No signature found``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:157
#: c6ae448372eb48498cf7a4d021e46674
msgid ""
"If the commit is signed, the key is downloaded from a GPG key server. If you "
"can see the following error message, please check if you have uploaded the "
"key to a key server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:159
#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:202
#: b4595ebd93134067b2e627c47f42916b a4c98c17f34a4b1c8fa5882852270dfb
msgid "``policy/qubesos/code-signing — Unable to verify (no valid key found)``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:164
#: f8de887614b940aab8f3bfc08e365a42
msgid "No Signature Found"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:169
#: 53e0321f049a420e81f87f972dab0413
msgid "In this case, you have several options to sign the commit:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:171
#: d722971f51344ce3bf110fd70b946e12
msgid ""
"Amend the commit and replace it with a signed commit. You can use this "
"command to create a new signed commit:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:178
#: 01f653a91ad24922b5687b6b57585cf6
msgid "This also rewrites the commit so you need to push it forcefully:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:186
#: 4bf4dff0b4ab47b39d33fb7e9e804c03
msgid ""
"Create a signed tag for the unsigned commit. If the commit is back in "
"history and you do not want to change it, you can create a signed tag for "
"this commit and push the signature. You can use the alias from above:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:194
#: 795f15b689d947d7a82468442e12051c
msgid ""
"Now, the signature checker needs to re-check the signature. Please comment "
"on the pull request that you would like to have the signatures checked again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:199
#: b67fe91a2099435f9ca28f5fa15da2f5
msgid "Unable To Verify"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:204
#: 249e3a58c4274a719e2a567998609502
msgid ""
"This means that the `signature-checker <https://github.com/marmarek/"
"signature-checker>`__ has found a signature for the commit but is not able "
"to verify it using the any key available. This might be that you forgot to "
"upload the key to a key server. Please upload it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:207
#: d4fbf4e63a6444139a614350d0bcd5af
msgid "Using PGP with Email"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/code/code-signing.rst:210
#: 42776628ed4b48f58da30a1ee76a23a1
msgid ""
"If you’re submitting a patch by emailing the :ref:`developer mailing list "
"<introduction/support:qubes-devel>`, simply sign your email with your PGP "
"key. One good way to do this is with a program like `Enigmail <https://"
"www.enigmail.net/>`__. Enigmail is a security addon for the Mozilla "
"Thunderbird email client that allows you to easily digitally encrypt and "
"sign your emails."
msgstr ""
